---
name: "Partner With Us"
title: "Partner for genetic screening in India | Lightening Lives"
description: "Three ways to partner with us for genetic screening in India: hospitals and diagnostic labs, public health programmes, and CSR foundations and NGOs."
label: Partner with us
kicker: "Institutional collaboration models"
h1: 'Partner with us. <span class="h-mark">Choose how we work together.</span>'
lead: "Diagnostic lab chains, hospitals, national health missions and CSR foundations partner with us to bring confirmed, affordable molecular diagnosis to the people who need it most."
proof:
  - { icon: "badge-check", text: "ICMR approved" }
  - { icon: "award", text: "Patents granted in India and Japan" }
  - { icon: "map-pin", text: "15 sites, 9 states and Delhi" }
notice: true
closing:
  h2: 'Tell us about your laboratory, <span class="h-mark">programme or community.</span>'
  body: "Tell us the condition you need to test for and where the testing will happen. We will take it from there."
  solid: { text: "Start a conversation", enquire: true }
  line: { text: "How the test works", href: "/technology/" }
tabs:
  - { id: "laboratories", icon: "hospital", label: "Laboratories and hospitals" }
  - { id: "programmes", icon: "landmark", label: "Public health programmes" }
  - { id: "funders", icon: "hand-heart", label: "CSR and NGOs" }
---
{#- Partner With Us (client review of 27 October 2026, plan 2026-11-05 Task 6; before it, the ways to
    partner were on /partners/, which is now the partner network and hands an old link to one of them
    on here). Where every "Partner with us" leads. The three doors under the opening; then one tab for
    each reader, a plain section each without script (src/js/site/tabs.js makes them tabs, the tab bar
    drawn here and hidden until then); how a partnership starts; the close. /partnerships/ and
    /programmes/ forward here (src/site/_data/forwards.json). -#}
{%- set arrow = '<svg aria-hidden="true" width="18" height="12" viewBox="0 0 18 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M1 6h15M11 1l5 5-5 5"/></svg>' %}
{%- from "doors.njk" import doorList with context %}
{%- from "model.njk" import testingModel %}
{%- from "faq.njk" import faq %}

  <!-- 1. The three ways to partner, under the opening, on its ice white -->
  <section id="start" class="section on-mist partner-start" aria-label="Three ways to partner">
    <div class="wrap">
      {{ doorList(true) }}
      <p class="doors-else">{% icon "message-circle" %}<span>Looking for something else? Research collaborations, custom test co-development or media enquiries: <a class="link" {{ { who: "other" } | enquire | safe }}>talk to us {{ arrow | safe }}</a></span></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. One tab for each reader -->
  <div class="partner-tabs bg-paper" data-tabs>
    <div class="tabbar-band"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="tabbar" data-tabbar role="tablist" aria-label="Ways to partner" hidden>
        {%- for t in tabs %}
        <button type="button" class="tab" role="tab" data-tab-for="{{ t.id }}" aria-controls="{{ t.id }}" aria-selected="{{ 'true' if loop.first else 'false' }}">{% icon t.icon %}<span>{{ t.label }}</span></button>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
    </div></div>

    <section id="laboratories" class="section bg-paper tab-panel" data-tab-label="Laboratories and hospitals" aria-labelledby="laboratories-h">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
          <h2 id="laboratories-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">Turn any basic PCR room <span class="h-mark">into a high-throughput genetic lab.</span></h2>
          <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">For standalone labs, lab chains and hospital laboratories.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="audience mt-12">
          <div>
            <h3 class="audience-h">What changes for your laboratory</h3>
            <ul class="ticks mt-5">
              <li>{% icon "flask-conical" %}<p><strong>Zero DNA extraction.</strong> A tiny punch from the card goes straight into the PCR tube: no extraction step, hours saved.</p></li>
              <li>{% icon "thermometer" %}<p><strong>Zero cold chain.</strong> Cards arrive at room temperature in ordinary envelopes from remote centres and clinics, with no leaking tubes or haemolysed samples to reject.</p></li>
              <li>{% icon "circle-check-big" %}<p><strong>One test instead of two.</strong> Screening and definitive molecular confirmation in a single run.</p></li>
              <li>{% icon "layers" %}<p><strong>High throughput.</strong> Dozens of cards in one run, with same-day turnaround.</p></li>
              <li>{% icon "stethoscope" %}<p><strong>Reports clinicians can act on.</strong> Affected patient, carrier (trait) or unaffected, without ambiguity.</p></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <aside class="audience-card" aria-labelledby="lab-needs-h">
            <span class="icon-tile">{% icon "microscope" %}</span>
            <h3 id="lab-needs-h" class="audience-h">What your laboratory needs</h3>
            <p>A thermal cycler, a gel tank, a card punch, and technicians who have run basic PCR or whom we train.</p>
            <a class="link" href="/technology/#laboratory">The full list {{ arrow | safe }}</a>
          </aside>
        </div>
        <h3 class="audience-h mt-12">How we work with you</h3>
        <ol class="flow mt-5">
          <li><span class="flow-n">1</span><p><strong>Scientific consultation.</strong> A call with our scientists to map the conditions and test volumes you serve.</p></li>
          <li><span class="flow-n">2</span><p><strong>Hands-on training.</strong> We set up the workflow in your laboratory and train and certify your bench staff.</p></li>
          <li><span class="flow-n">3</span><p><strong>Supply and support.</strong> A steady supply of LitLife™ tests, with ongoing technical and troubleshooting support.</p></li>
        </ol>
        <div class="audience-act">
          <a class="btn btn-line" {{ { who: "laboratory" } | enquire | safe }}>Talk to our scientific team</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="programmes" class="section bg-paper tab-panel" data-tab-label="Public health programmes" aria-labelledby="programmes-h">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
          <h2 id="programmes-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">Removing the three biggest bottlenecks <span class="h-mark">in public health screening.</span></h2>
          <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">Two-step screening loses patients, spends budget on cold chains and misses newborns. LitLife™ fixes all three.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="answers mt-12">
          <li>
            <span class="icon-tile">{% icon "user-x" %}</span>
            <p><strong>People lost between screening and confirmation.</strong> One test screens and confirms from the first finger-prick spot, so no family travels back for a second visit.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="icon-tile">{% icon "snowflake" %}</span>
            <p><strong>A cold chain from village to laboratory.</strong> Cards need no refrigeration: health workers send them from remote sub-centres to a district laboratory by ordinary post or courier.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="icon-tile">{% icon "baby" %}</span>
            <p><strong>Newborns discharged before testing.</strong> LitLife™ reads the DNA from a heel-prick spot at birth, with no 72-hour wait.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <h3 class="audience-h mt-12">How a programme runs</h3>
        {{ testingModel("mt-5") }}
        <div class="audience-foot mt-12">
          {%- set names = [] %}{% for st in work.states %}{% set names = (names.push(st.name), names) %}{% endfor %}
          <p class="audience-where">{% icon "map-pin" %}<span>Population and newborn screening at 15 sites in nine states and Delhi: {{ names.slice(0, -1).join(", ") }} and {{ names | last }}.</span></p>
          <div class="audience-act">
            <a class="btn btn-line" {{ { who: "programme" } | enquire | safe }}>Plan a public health programme</a>
            <a class="link" href="/our-work/">Explore our field work {{ arrow | safe }}</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="funders" class="section bg-paper tab-panel" data-tab-label="CSR and NGOs" aria-labelledby="funders-h">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
          <h2 id="funders-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">From testing <span class="h-mark">to complete care.</span></h2>
          <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">Your support delivers high-impact healthcare: a confirmed answer, counselling and care for every family.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="audience mt-12">
          <div>
            <h3 class="audience-h">Why it matters</h3>
            <ul class="ticks mt-5">
              <li>{% icon "circle-check-big" %}<p><strong>Every rupee reaches a definitive answer.</strong> Screening that stops at a possible case leaves families in limbo; one confirmatory test gives a life-changing answer at low cost.</p></li>
              <li>{% icon "megaphone" %}<p><strong>A camp that explains and tests.</strong> Awareness and genetic screening run together, collecting finger-prick spots while educating the community.</p></li>
              <li>{% icon "heart-handshake" %}<p><strong>Families are never left alone with a result.</strong> Every patient or carrier family is counselled, referred for prenatal diagnosis where needed, and linked to clinical care.</p></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="audience-faq">
            <h3 class="audience-h">Questions funders ask</h3>
            {{ faq([
              { q: "We are an NGO or foundation with no laboratory. Can we still run a screening programme?", a: "Yes. Your field volunteers or health workers collect a finger-prick spot on our barcoded card. The dried cards travel by ordinary courier to our laboratory, or a regional partner laboratory, for testing and reporting." },
              { q: "Do you help CSR funders design measurable programmes?", a: "Yes. We design end-to-end genetic health programmes with CSR teams and foundations, aligned with national priorities such as the National Sickle Cell Anaemia Elimination Mission and maternal and child health." },
              { q: "What happens to the children and carrier families a programme finds?", a: "Diagnosis is the beginning of care. Every patient is linked to local clinical treatment, and carrier couples receive genetic counselling and prenatal diagnostic support to plan future pregnancies." }
            ]) }}
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="audience-act">
          <a class="btn btn-line" {{ { who: "funder" } | enquire | safe }}>Fund or co-design a programme</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <!-- 3. How a partnership starts: four steps -->
  <section id="how-it-starts" class="section" aria-labelledby="how-it-starts-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="how-it-starts-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">How a partnership starts. <span class="h-mark">Four steps, from the first conversation.</span></h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">You bring the condition you need to screen for or diagnose. We bring the test, the method, the training and the counselling that follows a result.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="start-steps mt-12">
        <li><span class="icon-tile">{% icon "message-circle" %}</span><h3><span class="model-n">1</span> You tell us the need</h3><p>The condition and the setting: who will be tested, roughly how many, where samples will be collected and which laboratory will run them.</p></li>
        <li><span class="icon-tile">{% icon "clipboard-list" %}</span><h3><span class="model-n">2</span> We agree the scope</h3><p>What the test must detect, how results will be reported, and what training and counselling the programme needs.</p></li>
        <li><span class="icon-tile">{% icon "dna" %}</span><h3><span class="model-n">3</span> We develop or adapt the test</h3><p>A test we have, or a new one for the mutations your population carries.</p></li>
        <li><span class="icon-tile">{% icon "graduation-cap" %}</span><h3><span class="model-n">4</span> We train and stay with you</h3><p>Through reporting, counselling and follow-up.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>
